{
  "id": "luminous_efficacy",
  "title": "Luminous Efficacy",
  "description": "Calculate luminous efficacy and power requirements for various light sources. Luminous efficacy is the ratio of luminous flux (lumens) to power (watts), determining how efficiently a light source produces visible light.",
  "type": "datatable",
  "components": [
    {
      "type": "markdown",
      "content": "## Luminous Efficacy Calculator\n\n**Luminous Efficacy** (η) is the ratio of luminous flux to power:\n\n**η = Φ / P**\n\nWhere:\n- **η** = Luminous efficacy (lumens/W)\n- **Φ** = Luminous flux (lumens, lm)\n- **P** = Power (W)\n\nYou can also calculate required power: **P = Φ / η**"
    },
    {
      "type": "calculator",
      "inputs": [
        {
          "id": "luminous_flux",
          "label": "Luminous Flux",
          "type": "number",
          "unit": "lumens",
          "defaultValue": 500
        },
        {
          "id": "efficacy",
          "label": "Luminous Efficacy",
          "type": "number",
          "unit": "lumens/W",
          "defaultValue": 70
        }
      ],
      "outputs": [
        {
          "id": "power_required",
          "label": "Required Power",
          "formula": "inputs.luminous_flux / inputs.efficacy",
          "unit": "W",
          "format": "decimal"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "datatable",
      "headers": [
        "Light Type",
        "Luminous Efficacy Range (lumens/W)"
      ],
      "rows": [
        [
          "Fluorescent lamp",
          "45 - 75"
        ],
        [
          "Halogen lamp",
          "16 - 24"
        ],
        [
          "High pressure sodium vapor lamp",
          "85 - 150"
        ],
        [
          "LED lamp",
          "30 - 90"
        ],
        [
          "Mercury vapor lamp",
          "35 - 65"
        ],
        [
          "Metal halide lamp",
          "75 - 100"
        ],
        [
          "Tungsten incandescent light bulb lamp",
          "12 - 18"
        ]
      ]
    }
  ]
}